N1  - <p>BOINC criterion evidence - Abstract, verbatim: "BOINC (Berkeley Open Infrastructure for Network Computing) is an open-source framework for solving large-scale computational problems by means of public resource computing (PRC)." Abstract, verbatim: "Here, we present a new approach for performing large-scale parameter studies using COMSOL Multiphysics based on the BOINC technology." Introduction, verbatim: "With the help of BOINC [1, 6] it is possible to create and run self-made scientific applications heterogeneous computer networks." Figure 1: BOINC project named "Comsolwrapper." Figure 2: "Most of them are implemented by the BOINC framework." Section 2.2: "The ComsolGridStarter is a wrapper routine handling the BOINC client and BOINC user commands." | Full text: COMSOL Conference 2010, Paris | Link: ComsolGrid / BOINC | Source: COMSOL Conference (2010)ER&nbsp;&nbsp;-</p>
